  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Katiba: Empowering State Institutions &amp; Citizens on Access to informatio</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supports Protection of fundamental freedoms, in addition to access to information. Additionally, a significant amount of the information access initiatives will be carried out in partnership with the media.

The project seeks to enhance transparency and accountability and openness in government using access to information (law) to promote public participation in governance and prudent use of public resources. In line with the Constitution (of Kenya 2010), The project underscores the importance of the availability of information to ensure effective oversight of government functions by the public while noting that the failure to disclose information demonstrates disregard for the protection of human rights and fundamental freedoms provided for in the Constitution of Kenya 2010</narrative>
  </description>
